# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository.
#
# Why this matters here: the Transport Fever 3 base game ships its Lua sources
# with LF endings. With Git's default `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows, checking
# out or rebasing rewrites text files to CRLF, which makes the working tree differ
# from every installed/staged copy and produces noisy diffs.
#
# Rule: everything textual is stored and checked out as LF. Binary assets are
# left untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly textual
*.lua   text eol=lf
*.tl    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# Keep these binary (no line-ending conversion)
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.dds   binary
*.tga   binary
*.zip   binary
